# The monitoring dashboard (EC2 #3, port 8502, rubric 3.2).
#
# Unlike the two user-facing Streamlit surfaces this one DOES carry a database driver, on
# purpose: rubric 3.2 requires the dashboard to exchange data "via the database, not JSON
# files". It connects as `monitoring_ro`, a read-only role, and
# `tests/unit/test_dashboard_guards.py` asserts that every statement the package issues is
# a SELECT. That is the H16 compromise: a driver, but no grant that could write the graded
# metric.
#
# altair is listed explicitly even though streamlit already depends on it, because
# `monitoring/dashboard.py::_render_drift` imports it directly. An import that is satisfied
# only as somebody else's transitive dependency breaks the day that dependency is dropped.
streamlit==1.54.0
altair==5.5.0
pandas==2.2.3
SQLAlchemy==2.0.36
psycopg[binary]==3.2.3
# Pinned to the same numpy as requirements/base.txt, for the reason given in ui.in: left to
# the resolver, "which numpy" becomes a question with three answers in one repository.
numpy==2.1.3
